# Git Workflow

Repo: [`dustinestes/career-pipeline`](https://github.com/dustinestes/career-pipeline).

MUST: GitHub issue → branch → PR → human merges. Never commit to the default branch unless the user explicitly asks.

Before commit, push, or PR: ask **"Anything to add before I commit?"** and wait.
Do not commit, push, or create/close/comment on issues/PRs unless explicitly asked.

## Branch, commit, label

- Branch: `{type}/{issue}-{short-slug}`
- Commit: `{type}: {present-tense summary} (#{issue})`
- Issue: exactly **one** type label matching the commit prefix

```
✅ feat/12-yaml-config
   feat: add career-pipeline yaml schema (#12)
   label: feat

❌ branch: my-fixes / fix-stuff
❌ commit without (#N) or without an issue
❌ primary label: bug / enhancement (use fix / feat)
```

### GitHub type labels

Primary labels (must match commit/branch prefix):

`feat` | `fix` | `docs` | `chore` | `refactor` | `sec` | `breaking`

Do **not** use GitHub defaults `bug` or `enhancement` as the primary type label — use `fix` / `feat`. Triage labels (`help wanted`, `dependencies`, `question`, …) may accompany the type label.

Before creating or labeling an issue, ensure these seven labels exist on this repo (`gh label list`). If any are missing, create them:

```bash
gh label create feat --color 1D76DB --description "New feature or capability"
gh label create fix --color D73A4A --description "Bug fix"
gh label create docs --color 0075CA --description "Documentation"
gh label create chore --color 0E8A16 --description "Maintenance and repo organization"
gh label create refactor --color FBCA04 --description "Code or structure refactor"
gh label create sec --color B60205 --description "Security"
gh label create breaking --color E99695 --description "Breaking change"
```

## Local checks

Before push or opening a PR, run any repo checks that exist and fix failures locally. Do not rely on “CI will catch it.”

When CI is added, keep it green before merge.

## Docs in the same change

If the change affects skills, plugin `rules/`, schema, manifests, scripts, or install paths, update the relevant `docs/` (and `template/docs/` when workspace-facing) in the **same** change. Details: `.cursor/rules/docs-first.mdc`.

## PRs

PR body must include a GitHub closing keyword for the issue (e.g. `Closes #12`) so merge auto-closes it.

```
✅ One concern; PR body explains why
✅ `Closes #N` (or Fixes / Resolves) linking the issue
✅ Local checks green before push/PR

❌ Kitchen-sink PR
❌ PR with no closing keyword (leaves the issue open after merge)
```

Bootstrap exception: initial `main` seed commits may omit an issue number when the user explicitly requests the bootstrap push.
